  "body": "## Cause\r\n\r\nA 5-axis stamp path left its opening moves (before the first lean) without a pose. The post dump commanded zero angles only for a Z column after a lean. So the first move that the Fanuc post wrote with rotary words was the first tilted feed. The Fanuc angle memory (`rotAt`, `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`) was null, and the rate guard (`rotaryFeed`) refused the feed on `tilthead.mch` (A and B rates stated):\r\n\r\n```text\r\na feed that turns A from an angle the post does not know - the stated A rate cannot be held\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Fix (two sites, both small)\r\n\r\n1. `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/stamp.rs`: when a path leans anywhere, each station before the first lean states the upright Z column (`Some(UP)`). A path that never leans stays silent, as before.\r\n2. `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs` (`dump`): in a stream that leans, the first move that states the Z column commands explicit zero angles. Before, the zero came only after a lean.\r\n\r\nWhy both: the stamp alone does not help, because the dump wrote nothing for a stated Z column before a lean (the released claim on #3300 found this). The dump alone (zero on any first move) would guess an upright home for a move that states nothing. The guard forbids that guess. With the two parts, the post commands only a pose that the stream states. The rate guard is unchanged. A stream with no pose before its first tilted feed still refuses.\r\n\r\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3300-opening-rotary-pose.md` (chosen, why, dropped).\r\n\r\n## Opening blocks (Fanuc, tilthead.mch, 5-Axis Contour on the cap, clearance 20 mm, G54 at Z 50)\r\n\r\n| Before (origin/main) | After (this PR) |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| post refused: `a feed that turns A from an angle the post does not know - the stated A rate cannot be held` (no program) | `G43.4 H01` |\r\n| | `G00 Z-30.` |\r\n| | `G00 X0. Y-3.84 Z-30. A0. B0.` |\r\n| | `G01 X-0.776 Y-3.149 Z-47.314 A13.313 B15.42 F100` |\r\n\r\nBy the code (not posted in a test), main writes the same blocks without `A0. B0.` on a machine with no stated rate. The rotation then starts from an unknown angle. The order is: TCP on, retract to the clearance, the XY rapid at the clearance with A0 B0, then the approach. Flow5D: `G00 X-2.142 Y-6.642 Z-30. A0. B0.`. Swarf: `G00 X-24. Y-10.149 Z-25. A0. B0.`.\r\n\r\nNote: the approach feed (the G01 above) turns the rotaries while it descends to the first contact. That is the stamp's existing pose law, and it is not changed here. Filed as #3414 for a decision.\r\n\r\n## Tests (red on main, green here)\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-post` `opening_rotary_pose`:\r\n  - `a_leaning_stream_commands_zero_angles_on_its_first_upright_move`: red without the dump change (`no refusal: [\"a feed that turns A from an angle the post does not know - the stated A rate cannot be held\"]`), green with it.\r\n  - `a_stream_with_no_pose_before_its_first_tilted_feed_still_refuses`: the guard. A prismatic opening and a feed-first stream still refuse by name. Green before and after.\r\n  - `an_upright_stream_that_never_leans_commands_no_angles`: a stream that states only the Z column posts byte-identical to a stream with no axis, without G43.4.\r\n- `camcraft-app` `opening_rotary_pose` (generate on `tilthead.mch` + post with `fanuc.cps`):\r\n  - `contour5d_opening_states_rotaries_before_the_fanuc_tilted_feed`\r\n  - `flow5d_opening_states_rotaries_before_the_fanuc_tilted_feed`\r\n  - `swarf_opening_states_rotaries_before_the_fanuc_tilted_feed`\r\n  - All three red on main (the post refused; the opening stated no pose), green here.\r\n- Changed assertions (the law changed on purpose; the meaning \"no lean\" stays):\r\n  - `camcraft-motion` lib `multiaxis::stamp_tests::the_stamp_poses_only_moves_that_touch`: the opening rapid and the air feed now state the vertical axis instead of `None`.\r\n  - `camcraft-motion` `flow` `flow5d_states_an_axis_on_every_cut_move`: the check of the lead reads from the first lean.\r\n\r\nEach pinning test ran alone through `cargo xtask gate test <name> --crate <c> --binary opening_rotary_pose --exact`: all ok.\r\n\r\n## Goldens\r\n\r\nNo golden changed. `fanuc_posts_every_golden_byte_exact`, `recorded_streams` (incl. `golden/fanuc/rotary.nc`), `golden_cl`, `conformance` and `setup_align_multiaxis` are green with no update. 3-axis programs and the 3+2 streams that state their angles are byte-identical.\r\n\r\n## Gate results (debug)\r\n\r\nThe quick gate plan had 157 steps (over about 80), so I ran the touched binaries plus the golden and post suites:\r\n\r\n- `camcraft-post`: all 115 test binaries ok (incl. lib, `fanuc_post`, `recorded_streams`, `post_engine`, `script_fanuc`, `script_doosan_dnm`, `g93_feed`, `first_traverse_clearance*`).\r\n- `camcraft-motion`: lib 536 tests ok (after the assertion update), `flow`, `pivot5d`, `ruling`, `swarf_pose_continuity` ok.\r\n- `camcraft-app` (24 binaries, 206 tests, all ok): `opening_rotary_pose`, `setup_align_multiaxis`, `center_cut_multiaxis`, `golden_cl`, `conformance`, `rotary_feed_cap`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `posting_rotaries_first`, `doosan_dnm_a_state`, `microarc_test_part`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `first_4axis_part`, `tilt_a180`, `tilt_a180_routes`, `posed_contact`, `tormach_wrapped_a`, `tormach_fourth_axis`, `c_axis_live`, `wire_stamp`, `example_catalog`, `tilted_gouge_kinds`, `first_traverse_posed`, `first_traverse_rotary`, `section_mode`. Also `operations` filtered to `5d` / `swarf`: 8 ok.\r\n- Clippy `-D warnings`: `-p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-post --all-targets` clean; `-p camcraft-app --test opening_rotary_pose` clean.\r\n\r\n## Heavy lanes (#2568)\r\n\r\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main` on head 0d7263ac4 (release, `--ignored`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`): 242 steps, 0 failed, wall 77.5 min.\r\n\r\n- heavy build (release --no-run): ok.\r\n- motion heavy: all lanes ok (lib, bins, doc and the integration lanes, incl. `multiaxis`, `multiaxis_avoid`, `multiaxis_rough`, `flow`, `pivot5d`, `finish3d`, `rotary_adaptive`). The two known fails of #1950 are red as expected.\r\n- app heavy: all lanes ok (lib, bins, doc and the integration lanes, incl. `golden_cl`, `conformance`, `operations`, `first_traverse_posed`, `first_traverse_rotary`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `c_axis_live`, `wire_stamp`, `verify`, `tilt_stock_cap`, `tilt_basis_compat`). The known fails of #1950 and #2849 are red as expected.\r\n- Not run: none of the reached lanes.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- Posts other than Fanuc. I checked which posts keep an angle memory with `rotaryFeed`: `fanuc.cps` and `doosan-dnm.cps`. The fix is in the dump, so Doosan gets the same zero words. No Doosan five-axis program was posted in a test. `fanuc-lathe.cps` uses `rotaryFeedCap` and has no angle memory.\r\n- The #2870 catalog script (`camcraft-cli script build.camscript` on mkinney's branch) was not run. The app tests use the same machine, tool, part and three operations.\r\n- `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs` was already over 400 lines (725); this PR adds 9 lines.\r\n- Overlap: open PR #3306 changes `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` (line 46) and no longer `post/mod.rs`. No textual overlap with this PR.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A five-axis path that leans now posts A0 B0 on its opening move at the clearance, so the Fanuc post no longer refuses the first tilted feed on a machine with stated rotary rates.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #3300\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
